ZERO CACHE


Method 1: Using Group Policy (Recommended)
This is the most efficient way to apply the setting across multiple machines in a domain.

Open the Group Policy Management Console (gpmc.msc).

Create a new GPO or edit an existing one linked to the desired Organizational Unit (OU).

Navigate to:
Computer Configuration > Windows Settings > Security Settings > Local Policies > Security Options

Locate the policy: Interactive logon: Number of previous logons to cache (in case domain controller is not available).

Check Define this policy setting and set the value to 0.

Run gpupdate /force on the target machines to apply the change.





