SMART CARD LOCKOUT

Step 1: Configuration via GPO (The Domain Level)
To apply this across the board, you use the Default Domain Policy:

Open Group Policy Management (gpmc.msc).

Expand your forest and domain, right-click Default Domain Policy, and select Edit.

Navigate to:

Computer Configuration > Policies > Windows Settings > Security Settings > Local Policies > Security Options

Find the policy: Interactive logon: Require smart card (In newer versions of Windows, it may be labeled Interactive logon: Require Windows Hello for Business or smart card).

Set it to Enabled.

Click Apply and OK



