FORCE GPO UPDATE


Method 1: Group Policy Management Console (GUI)
This is the easiest way to target an entire Organizational Unit (OU) at once.

Open Group Policy Management (gpmc.msc).

Right-click the OU containing the computers you want to update.

Select Group Policy Update....

A confirmation window will appear showing how many computers are in that OU. Click Yes.

What happens next: Windows will remotely schedule a task on every computer in that OU to run gpupdate /force within the next 0 to 10 minutes. This staggered start prevents your network from being slammed by every PC hitting the DC at the exact same second.



